[?25l> Let me analyze the C code behavior:

Key observations:
- scanf("%d ", &time_stamp) — reads an integer, then skips trailing whitespace (including newlines)
- scanf("%8[A-Z0-9] %6[A-Z0-9] ", ...) — reads up to 8 chars matching [A-Z0-9], skips whitespace, reads up to 6 chars matching [A-Z0-9], skips whitespace
- scanf("%3[A-Z] %3[A-Z]", ...) — reads 3 uppercase letters, skips whitespace, reads 3 more
- scanf("%80[^\n]", comments) — reads up to 80 chars until newline (optional, comments start as empty)
- Each scanf returns EOF check → break
- Linked list sorted by time_stamp (insertion sort)
- supersedes: a directive is superseded if a later directive in the list has the same luggage_id and same departure
- matches: - is a wildcard, otherwise exact string match
- printf("%010u ...") — 10-digit zero-padded unsigned int
- Args check: exactly 4 args (argc != 5 → error to stderr, exit(1))
- exit(0) at end
